  "details": "Recalibrating after having already calibrated while using the --freeze-tracking-on-disconnect launch option will cause odd calibration behavior for certain avatars. Specifically, the whole avatar seems to have been shifted downwards, then the armature pulled up, resulting in a \"tip-toe\" T-pose. In this broken calibration pose, rotating the arms will also rotate the avatar's arms slightly, which doesn't happen in normal calibration. Finishing calibration will lock the feet into the extreme pointed toe pose. Toggling the avatar measurement method will fix the calibration once. Calibrating on an avatar that does not exhibit this behavior then switching to an avatar that does will not result in the pointed toes. \nThis behavior happens even with a single tracker (see gif with the raising leg). \nExample avatars that exhibits this issue: \n- avtr_a75de73e-0ddf-4c9b-af62-4d899ceaf61b\n- avtr_863817e6-2bc1-489c-9ccd-895269203827\nIn very rare instances certain avatars will just refuse to be IK tracked after calibration. (not sure how to reproduce, but happened multiple times during testing. Possibly related to setting the calibration range lower than 0.6 in combination to whatever is causing this).",
